Title: Do not pass --gc-sections when linking for AROS
Repository: libarchive 3.8.11 (release archive)
Date: 2026-11-16
Author: aros-libresprite project
Problem: CMakeLists.txt adds -Wl,--gc-sections for every system except Darwin and SunOS. AROS executables are relocatable ELF objects without an entry symbol; ld then fails with "gc-sections requires either an entry or an undefined symbol", so every configure link check fails and configuration stops (pid_t "doesn't exist").
Change: Treat AROS like SunOS: no section garbage collection flags.
Scope: all AROS targets
Upstream: https://github.com/libarchive/libarchive/pull/3861 (open, submitted 2026-11-16)
Verification: libarchive configures and builds for mainline x86_64 (scripts/deps.py)
Removal: when libarchive excludes AROS itself
---
diff --color -ru libarchive-3.8.11/CMakeLists.txt b/CMakeLists.txt
--- a/CMakeLists.txt	2026-10-30 21:34:55
+++ b/CMakeLists.txt	2026-11-16 10:53:40
@@ -142,8 +142,9 @@
   IF(CMAKE_SYSTEM_NAME MATCHES "Darwin")
     SET(CMAKE_EXE_LINKER_FLAGS "${CMAKE_EXE_LINKER_FLAGS} -Wl,-dead_strip")
     SET(CMAKE_SHARED_LINKER_FLAGS "${CMAKE_SHARED_LINKER_FLAGS} -Wl,-dead_strip")
-  ELSEIF(CMAKE_SYSTEM_NAME MATCHES "SunOS")
-    # SunOS linker doesn't support --gc-sections
+  ELSEIF(CMAKE_SYSTEM_NAME MATCHES "SunOS|AROS")
+    # SunOS linker doesn't support --gc-sections. AROS executables are
+    # relocatable objects without an entry point, which --gc-sections refuses.
   ELSE()
     # Place the functions and data into separate sections, allowing the linker
     # to garbage collect the unused ones.
